ghast ## flies and floats every tick (travel 20 000 instr per ghast and tick: a mover, not a rest cost)
turtle ## swims every tick (amphibious mode: travel and move control per tick)
slime ## bounds: every creature is in the air or on a bound most ticks
magma_cube ## same as the slime
rabbit ## bounds along its path (hop mode)
silverfish ## wanders and searches paths (pathfind 100 000 instr per search, 3 per tick at 2 000)
enderman ## goals asked at the vanilla cadence (1/10 per tick): arbitrate visits 10 % of the herd per tick
zoglin ## walks all the time (18 visits of travel per tick at 2 000)
phantom ## circles and dives all the time (a flier moves by `Bank`/`Direct`); Mob 40 170 vs ECS 8 669 per creature and tick
vex ## flies at a random point and charges all the time; Mob 26 757 vs ECS 1 942
cave_spider ## the climb wish never ends: the Mob pushes at the CORNER of the target block (0.707 from its centre) and the cave spider's width is 0.7, so `closerToCenterThan(width)` never holds (vanilla's own quirk); the tick is ~240 instr per wish
dolphin ## swims every tick (the smooth control and the travel of the water run each tick: a mover; 1 360 instr per creature and tick, as the turtle's)
axolotl ## swims every tick (same control and travel as the dolphin)
drowned ## swims every tick (its control and the travel of the water run each tick)
bee ## the six asks of its cycle (enter, validate x2, pollinate, locate, go to hive, known flower) come every 20 to 40 ticks per bee (conditions of state, no event yet): 775 instr per creature and tick; the Mob asks each goal every second tick
